Source code for running analysis

# Untargeted Metabolomics (src/untargeted/)

Untargeted metabolomics processing, quality control, and statistical analysis
of human developing cortical tissue (n = 24, gestational weeks 16–24). 

## Script Run Order

| Order | Script | Description |
|-------|--------|-------------|
| 1 | `Filtering.Rmd` | Sample outlier removal, retention time filtering, duplicate resolution, missingness filtering |
| 2 | `Exogenous_Flagging.Rmd` | Flag and remove instrument contaminants and environmental exposures |
| 3 | `Clean_Visualization.Rmd` | Peak intensity, detection, missingness, abundance, variability, and PCA |
| 4 | `Sex_and_GW_Analysis.Rmd` | GW correlation, GW/sex limma, sex Wilcoxon, PLS-DA, UpSet overlap |
| 5 | `Pathway_Analysis.Rmd` | MSEA (fgsea) and ORA using KEGG, Reactome, and WikiPathways |
| 6 | `Neurotransmitter_Analysis.Rmd` | Subgroup analysis on neurotransmitter-related metabolites |
| 7 | `Steroid_Analysis.Rmd` | Subgroup analysis on steroid-related metabolites |
| 8 | `Analysis_Summary.Rmd` | Cross-analyses summary of significant and nominal hits |

## Standalone Scripts

| Script | Description |
|--------|-------------|
| `Single_Metabolite_Profile.R` | Generates a 4-panel profile figure for any single metabolite (sex comparison, GW trajectory, analysis summary tile) |

## Shared Function Files

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `functions.R` | Data preparation, abundance/variability calculation, plotting, trajectory visualization |
| `filtering_functions.R` | Sample and metabolite filtering functions (outlier removal, RT filtering, duplicate detection) |
| `missingness_visualization_functions.R` | Missingness distribution plots (overall and by sex) |

## Key Outputs

All outputs are written to `results/untargeted/`.

| Directory | Contents |
|-----------|----------|
| `untargeted_filtering/` | Intermediate filtering diagnostics and CSVs |
| `untargeted_clean/` | Cleaned dataset figures, analysis result CSVs |
| `untargeted_steroids/` | Steroid subgroup analysis results |
| `untargeted_neurotransmitters/` | Neurotransmitter subgroup analysis results |
| `profiles/` | Single-metabolite profile figures |

# Targeted Hormones (src/targeted/)
LC-MS/MS quantification of testosterone (TT), 17B-estradiol (E2), and progesterone (P4)

## Script Run Order

| Order | Script | Description |
|-------|--------|-------------|
| 1 | `corr_age_hormones.Rmd` | Outlier detection, GW–hormone linear/polynomial model comparison, hormone-hormone Pearson correlations |
| 2 | `Exogenous_Flagging.Rmd` | Sex differences in hormone concentrations, receptor Kd reference, literature comparison|

## Key Outputs
All outputs are written to `results/targeted/`.

| Directory | Contents |
|-----------|----------|
| `age_analysis_plots/` | GW–hormone LOESS, linear, and polynomial fit figures |
| `hormone_hormone_correlation_plots/` | Pairwise hormone scatter plots (by sex, by GW) |
| `sex_comparison_plots/` | Distribution histograms, sex-comparison boxplots, literature comparison panels |
| `untargeted_neurotransmitters/` | Neurotransmitter subgroup analysis results |
| `hormone_csv/` | Correlation summary, sex comparison stats |

## Gene-Hormone Analysis (src/gene-hormone/)
Pseudobulk limma-voom association of gonadal hormone concentrations with snRNA-seq gene expression across cortical cell types (n = 24, GW 16–24).
Testosterone is analyzed in males only; estradiol and progesterone are sex-combined with sex as covariate. Each hormone is tested at three annotation levels (celltype, subclass, class).


## Script Run Order

| Order | Script | Description |
|-------|--------|-------------|
| 1 | `filter_recluster.R` | Note: Run as a separate job, not in an interactive RStudio session. Filter snRNA-seq data, remove absent samples, Harmony recluster | REQUIRES data/SSD_RNAonly.rds
| 2 | `prep_data.R` | Cache pseudobulk aggregates, batch proportions, Seurat subsets |
| 3 | `QC_UMAP_plots.qmd` | Cell type QC tables and UMAP visualizations |
| 4 | `Gene_Covariate_Testing.qmd` | Covariate regression (GW, cell count, sex, batch fraction) |
| 5 | `pseudobulk_cell_comparison.qmd` | Determine optimal pseudobulking group size |
| 6 | `receptor_expression.qmd` | Hormone receptor gene expression across cell types |
| 7 | `testosterone_gene_limma.qmd` | TT–gene limma-voom (celltype) |
| 8 | `testosterone_gene_limma_class.qmd` | TT–gene limma-voom (class) |
| 9 | `testosterone_gene_limma_subclass.qmd` | TT–gene limma-voom (subclass) |
| 10 | `estradiol_progesterone_gene_limma.qmd` | E2/P4–gene limma-voom (celltype) |
| 11 | `estradiol_progesterone_gene_limma_class.qmd` | E2/P4–gene limma-voom (class) |
| 12 | `estradiol_progesterone_gene_limma_subclass.qmd` | E2/P4–gene limma-voom (subclass) |
| 13 | `targeted_gene_list_limma.qmd` | Limma-voom on subset of gene-lists from hormone gene expression studies |
| 14 | `gene_list_scatter.R` | Scatter plots for gene list hits |

## Shared Function Files

| File | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `pseudobulk_functions.R` | pseudobulk aggregation,
limma-voom wrappers, hormone metadata merging, plotting functions |

## Key Outputs
All outputs are written to `results/gene-hormone/`.

| Directory | Contents |
|-----------|----------|
| `qc/, umap/` | Cell type QC tables and UMAP figures |
| `covariate_analysis/` | Covariate regression results and volcano plots |
| `cell_comparison/` | Pseudobulk comparison |
| `testosterone_genes/` | TT–gene limma results (celltype) |
| `testosterone_genes_class/, testosterone_genes_subclass/` | TT results at class/subclass level |
| `estradiol_genes/, progesterone_genes/` | E2/P4 limma results (celltype) |
| `estradiol_genes_class/, progesterone_genes_class/, estradiol_genes_subclass/, progesterone_genes_subclass/` | E2/P4 at class/subclass level |
| `single_cell_plots_analysis_celltypes/` | Receptor gene expression cell-type figures |
|`targeted_gene_list/` | Results from literature gene-list hypothesis driven analysis |
| `gene_list_scatter/` | Per-hormone gene list scatter PDFs |
